---
// What the site is, how it is built, and who built it (#544). The footer's
// "Ajay Thakur" is the way in, from every route.
//
// NO ISLAND, SO NO TOPBAR. The Topbar mounts the search overlay and the trail
// count — 73,225 B gzipped on /concepts, which has nothing else — for a page
// of prose, and #544 says plainly that no islands are added. So this page is budgeted at
// zero in perf-budget.json, like `/`, and an island here has to argue for
// itself in a pull request rather than arrive. The eyebrow is the way back to
// the graph — as the eyebrow is the way back up on a domain page — and the page
// ends on two more ways in, so it is not a dead end (CLAUDE.md §1).
//
// WHERE THE THREAD RUNS HERE: it does not, for the reason it does not run
// through /concepts (CLAUDE.md §5). The thread is the path a reader takes
// through the graph; this page is about the graph rather than a step in it.
//
// THE COUNTS ARE READ FROM THE CONTENT AT BUILD, NOT WRITTEN HERE. A number
// typed into prose goes stale with the next batch — PLAN.md §8 tells that story
// (#319).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
import { allNodes } from '../lib/content';
import { directory, domainRoutes, tally } from '../lib/directory';

const groups = directory(allNodes);
const totals = tally(groups);
const domains = domainRoutes(groups).length;

const REPO = 'https://github.com/opendroid/the-infinity';
const GPL = 'https://the-gpl.com';
const GITHUB = 'https://github.com/opendroid';

const PROSE = 'mt-3 max-w-[62ch] text-[15px] leading-[1.65] text-starlight';
const LINK = 'text-thread underline underline-offset-2';
---

<Base
  title="About · theinfinity.ai"
  description="What theinfinity.ai is, how it is built, and who built it."
>
  {/*
    The handoff's landing padding — 56px over 52px, 36px over 40px on a phone —
    rather than the 12px the directory pages leave under their Topbar: with no
    bar above it, this page starts at the top edge. Written in px because this
    repo's spacing scale is keyed by pixel value, so `py-12` is 12px, not 3rem.
  */}
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-[680px] px-[26px] pb-[52px] pt-[56px] max-md:pb-[40px] max-md:pt-[36px]">
    <Eyebrow>
      {/*
        A real 24px box, for the reason the domain page's eyebrow link is one:
        at the eyebrow's own 11px it would be a standalone control under the
        WCAG 2.2 AA 2.5.8 minimum. The negative margin gives the height back to
        the layout so the heading does not move.
      */}
      <a href="/" class="-my-[7px] inline-flex min-h-[24px] items-center text-dust no-underline hover:text-starlight">
        theinfinity.ai
      </a>
    </Eyebrow>
    <h1 class="mt-1.5 font-display text-[30px] font-semibold leading-[1.16] text-starlight max-md:text-[23px]">
      About
    </h1>

    <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-[62ch] text-[15px] leading-[1.65] text-dust">
      A concept graph for AI and machine learning: {totals.concepts} concepts across {domains} domains,
      each one a page you can read at three depths.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-[34px]">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-dust">What it is</h2>
      <p class={PROSE}>
        Every concept is one page with a 30-second intuition, an engineer's view and the math — the same
        idea three ways, switched in place — plus a figure and typed edges to what it requires, what it
        unlocks and what sits alongside it. Follow an edge and the site keeps the path you took as a
        trail you can share.
      </p>
      <p class={PROSE}>
        Each concept carries a trust tier. Verified means a person read the page and merged it; frontier
        means it was drafted from the sources it cites and is waiting for that review. Both cite primary
        sources.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-[34px]">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-dust">How it's built</h2>
      <p class={PROSE}>
        The graph is content as code. Every concept is a JSON file in{' '}
        <a href={REPO} class={LINK}>the repository</a>, validated against a schema, and it changes only
        when a pull request is merged — the merge is the act of verification. Concepts are drafted, and
        the code is written, with Claude Code at authoring time; nothing on the site calls a language
        model.
      </p>
      <p class={PROSE}>
        Pages are pre-rendered with Astro and served from Firebase Hosting's CDN, so a concept reads
        without JavaScript. Small React islands add the depth toggle, the figures, the mini-map and the
        trail, and search runs in the browser against a static index. A Go API on Cloud Run answers the
        mini-map, suggests the nearest concepts when one is missing, and keeps shared trails and
        requests in Firestore.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-[34px]">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-dust">Who built it</h2>
      {/*
        DRAFT (#544). Ajay edits this paragraph before the pull request merges;
        an agent wrote it from what the repository says about itself. Nothing
        else on this page depends on its wording.
      */}
      <p class={PROSE}>
        Ajay Thakur builds theinfinity.ai in the open, as a learning project and a portfolio piece. He
        also made <a href={GPL} class={LINK}>the-gpl.com</a>, chapters and demos on Go. The rest of his
        work is on <a href={GITHUB} class={LINK}>GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-8 border-t border-line pt-6 text-[14px] text-dust">
      <a href="/concepts" class={LINK}>Browse every concept</a>, or{' '}
      <a href="/" class={LINK}>start from the beginning of the thread</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
